 this either way.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Joni Ernst (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Iowa's Senate seat is open with Joni Ernst retiring, and the race between Republican Ashley Hinson and Democrat Josh Turek is one of the cycle's closest. Most forecasters rate it a Tossup, with one calling it Tilt R and another Lean D. Recent polls are scattered: a late-September Marist survey showed Turek up eight, while several Republican-sponsored polls had the race tied or Hinson slightly ahead. Averages put Turek up roughly one to two points.\n\nHinson holds a clear cash-on-hand advantage, but Turek has drawn heavy outside spending in his favor. Prediction markets lean toward Hinson, reflecting Iowa's Republican baseline. The race sits on a knife's edge heading into the final weeks, with fuel prices and foreign policy emerging as flashpoints.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6012, "margin": 1.25}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5782, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5857, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5846, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4983, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.503, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.579, "margin": 0.8}]}